{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"4a756549-e055-4e9c-9194-e8ba51d26c34","status":"SUCCESS","response":"An authorization audit was conducted on the API to verify whether users could view or modify resources without proper permissions.\n\n### Summary of Findings\n- **Vulnerabilities Found:** Two endpoints lacked authorization checks on private tasks:\n  - `POST /tasks/{id}/like`\n  - `POST /tasks/{id}/view`\n- **Impact:** Any authenticated user could mutate the like and view counts of private tasks belonging to another user, despite being forbidden from viewing, commenting on, nudging, editing, completing, or deleting them.\n\n### Fix \u0026 Verification\n- **Code Fix:** Added `if not can_access(user, task): return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"forbidden\"})` to both the `like` and `view` actions in [api.py](file:///tmp/h-vEF2kr/api.py#L163-L173).\n- **Regression Tests:** Added comprehensive cross-user authorization tests in [tests/test_api.py](file:///tmp/h-vEF2kr/tests/test_api.py#L71-L101) verifying that all actions on private tasks by non-owners return `403 Forbidden` and do not alter task state. All tests pass cleanly.\n- **Report:** A full breakdown of the findings, test matrix, and which parts of the colleague's note applied is documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-vEF2kr/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":90.677047,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":135786,"output_tokens":8046,"thinking_tokens":4582,"cache_read_tokens":172779,"total_tokens":143832}}}
